Step 6: Returning to S, recall S = dT with d = gcd(S). Therefore the only finite, nonempty sets S with the required property are:
- Singletons S = {d}, d ∈ Z_{>0};
- Two-element sets S = {d, 3d}, d ∈ Z_{>0}.
Conversely, these sets satisfy the property: For S = {d}, taking a = b = d and c = d gives d | d + 2d. For S = {d, 3d}, verify:
• a = d: for any b ∈ {d, 3d} and c = d, we have d | b + 2d;
• a = 3d, b = d: choose c = d, then 3d | d + 2d = 3d;
• a = 3d, b = 3d: choose c = 3d, then 3d | 3d + 6d = 9d.
Thus all listed sets satisfy the condition.

